messages:
Emily: Heads-up — bank POC scheduled Tue. They require websocket streaming (low-latency), function/tool calling with structured JSON outputs (schema validation), and traffic must traverse their corporate proxy (mTLS). Also flagged pricing + Dedicated availability. Can we confirm a short runbook and who joins the call?

Ivan: We can demo websocket streaming + function calls. High-level notes: streaming function_call events come as incremental events and final args are emitted as JSON. Prefer the Node SDK websocket for the demo. Example (very small):
```js
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.redwood.com/v1/stream');
ws.onopen = () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    model: 'rwd-stream-1',
    input: 'Process invoice',
    functions: [{ name: 'createInvoice', parameters: { amount: 'number', id: 'string' } }]
  }));
};
ws.onmessage = (ev) => {
  const pkt = JSON.parse(ev.data);
  if (pkt.type === 'function_call') handlePartial(pkt);
  if (pkt.type === 'finish') handleFinal(pkt);
};
```
Streaming delivers token deltas and function_call frames; buffer args until finish. Also recommend prefix caching for repeated prompts to reduce token costs.

Marta: For structured output please use explicit function defs + JSON schema. I'll attach a sample function spec and a small eval harness to validate output shape. About the proxy: customer expects mTLS + SNI routing. In our experience that usually means either Dedicated with VPC peering or Private deployment (customer-managed egress). Hosted can work for demos if they allow outbound websockets through their proxy.

Dennis: Security checklist for the buyer: SOC2 attestation, network architecture diagram, data retention policy, and the security questionnaire. Link to our security portal: https://redwood.example.com/sec-portal. For mTLS we need certificate exchange instructions and their proxy IPs for allowlisting. If they require HSM/KMS integration for keys, that pushes toward Private.

Alex: Pricing quick notes: hosted websocket streaming is billed per token + small streaming surcharge; Dedicated is committed capacity (flat throughput pricing) + overage. For short POC demos we can provide credits to cover streaming minutes. If they expect sustained 24/7 traffic or >1000 QPS, recommend Dedicated for unit cost predictability. I'll DM sample numbers for the account.

Emily: Excellent. Request: create a 1-page runbook with fallback plan if websocket is blocked (e.g., fallback to chunked HTTP streaming or long-polling), sample code for both websocket and REST streaming, and a checklist of artifacts (SOC2, network diagram, cert exchange, pricing sheet). Who can own the runbook and join Wed 10am PT call?

Ivan: I'll own the runbook and be on the call. Quick fallback snippet for REST chunked streaming and function_call assembly (Python pseudocode):
```python
buffer = ''
for chunk in rest_stream():
    if chunk['type'] == 'function_call':
        buffer += chunk['args']
    elif chunk['type'] == 'finish':
        args = json.loads(buffer)
        call_function(args)
        buffer = ''
```
If websocket is blocked by proxy, long-polling with chunked transfer-encoding usually works.

Marta: I'll own the demo artifacts (function specs + structured-output tests) and prep slides. Adding Emily and Ivan to the invite. :thumbsup:

Emily: Thanks team — please drop runbook + pricing into the calendar invite and tag me. Also tagging Dennis to confirm the questionnaire items on the invite.

Dennis: Got it, I'll upload the questionnaire and network checklist before the call.

Emily: /cc @Alex — expect follow-up on pricing numbers in the invite.

(End of thread)
